ary of Third Federal Savings and Loan Association of Cleveland, MHC.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Marc A. Stefanski | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 71 | Compensation: $3.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["TFS Financial Corporation is a mid-cap financial services business with a $4.3B market cap on $321M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $71M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 22 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.91\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.5%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 155% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.5501826205532092},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (20.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":